{
  "base_commit": "7dc50894695b7c37c9a3ec4f2d1d5bfcdfcc545c",
  "doc": "I49 prereg instrument (seal protocol (c)): the rule catalog the held-out run uses is the catalog at the base commit, holon-rules/1.15 (holon.rules.catalog_version('M3') there, the newest key of holon.rules.CATALOGS). Its producers reach far beyond holon/rules/ through lazy imports, so the pin is every file under holon/ at the base commit, by the sha256 of its bytes. After the seal opens, a change to any pinned file, and any file added under holon/, counts for no held-out result unless spec/M4/lib/heldout_disclosures.jsonl discloses it (path, phase pre_seal or post_seal, why, affects); every result a post_seal change affects carries I49's contamination caveat (tests_m4/test_i49_heldout.py R5). tree_sha256: sha256 over sorted (path, NUL, sha256 bytes).",
